 "notes": "Combined (thick blue) 95% C.L. exclusion limit from Fig. 4 (e-print Fig5.jpg), GrAHal pathfinding run around the TM010 mode at 6.375 GHz (6.3744-6.3753 GHz, m_a ~ 26.37 ueV). Figure gives g/g_KSVZ vs frequency; converted with g_KSVZ = (alpha/2pi)(1.92)/f_a and m_a = 5.7 ueV x (1e12 GeV/f_a), giving g_KSVZ ~ 1.03e-14 GeV^-1 at 26.37 ueV, consistent with the paper's quoted minimum g_agamma <= 2.2e-13 GeV^-1 = 22 x g_KSVZ. Paper assumed axions make up all the local DM density of 0.450 GeV/cm^3 (stated in LaTeX source), so no density rescaling applied. Digitised via pixel analysis of the raster figure, gridline-calibrated; the thin individual tuning-step curves were excluded, keeping the combined envelope.",
